					<div class="uv-content">
						


            

 


        
        





        









 












                                                                                                                                 
        <div class="row uv-sect bg--yellow text--black">
            <div class="col-12">
                                                                                                                                                                         Searching for housing in a new city, and especially a new country, can be challenging. Whether you choose to live in residence or off campus, take time to think about what type of accommodation will best suit your needs.
                                                        </div>
        </div>
                                                                                                                                                  
        <div class="row uv-sect bg--dark-blue text--white">
            <div class="col-12">
                                    <h2 id="ipn-on-campus-housing">On-campus housing</h2>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                         <p>There are a variety of on-campus housing options for students.</p>
<p>Visit&#160;<a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/residence/index.php">Residence Services</a> to find out what's available and apply online. Space is limited, so apply as soon as possible.</p>
                                                        </div>
        </div>
                                                                                                                                                  
        <div class="row uv-sect bg--linear-top">
            <div class="col-12">
                                    <h2 id="ipn-off-campus-housing">Off-campus housing</h2>
                                                                                                                                                                         <p>Searching for housing in a new city, and especially a new country, can be challenging. If you plan to live off campus, it will be important to familiarize yourself with the available options, understand some key considerations, and know how to avoid scams.</p>
                                                                                                                
    <div class="btn-row">
                                                                                                          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="off-campus-housing/index.php">Learn more about off-campus housing</a>
        
                </div>
                                        </div>
        </div>
                                                                                                                                                  
        <div class="row uv-sect bg--linear-top">
            <div class="col-12">
                                    <h2 id="ipn-transportation">Transportation</h2>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             <h3>Transit system</h3>
<p>UVic is a&#160;<a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/sustainability/topics/transportation/transit/index.php">major transit hub</a>.&#160;Plan your commute on <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.bctransit.com/victoria/home">Victoria's transit system</a> which operates 7 days a week, 365 days a year.</p>
<p>Most students registered in at least one on-campus course for credit will be enrolled in the <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/students/campus-services/transportation-parking/student-bus-pass/index.php">U-Pass program</a>.</p>
                                                                                                                                        <div class="alert alert-info">
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     <p>Starting September 2023, you'll need to use the new Umo mobile app or a reloadable Umo card to show proof of payment on all buses in the Victoria Regional Transit System. The UVic ONECard will no longer operate as your bus pass.</p>
<p>You'll need to activate your U-Pass every term with that term's unique-to-you <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://mybuspass.uvic.ca/rpt/uvon/r/mybuspass/home?session=14136108547863">UVic benefit code</a>.</p>
<p>For more information on how to activate and use your U-Pass, visit the <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/students/campus-services/transportation-parking/student-bus-pass/index.php">U-Pass program website</a>.</p>
                                </div>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 <h4>Exchange and visiting research students</h4>
<p>Exchange and visiting research students are not automatically enrolled in the U-Pass program. You can opt in by purchasing a <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://uvss.ca/u-pass/">University of Victoria Students' Society</a> or <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://gss.uvic.ca/about-gss/services/bus-pass/">Graduate Students' Society</a> membership package.</p>
<p>If you prefer not to purchase a UVSS or GSS membership, you can access the transit system using cash, purchase tickets from a <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.bctransit.com/victoria/fares/where-to-buy/">fare product vendor</a>, or pay via <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.bctransit.com/umo/">Umo</a> which is a contactless fare payment system. To use Umo, you can download the Umo app or get a free reloadable Umo card from <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.bctransit.com/victoria/fares/where-to-buy/">fare product vendors</a> around Victoria. On campus, the UVSS, GSS, and UVic Campus Pharmacy can provide Umo cards.&#160;You can then buy a pass or load cash through the app, online at&#160;<a class="icoa icoa--out" href="http://ca.umopass.com/"><strong>ca.umopass.com</strong></a>, at a vendor location, or through Umo&#8217;s customer service toll-free at 877-380-8181.</p>
<h3>Cycling</h3>
<p>Visit our&#160;<a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/sustainability/topics/transportation/cycling/index.php">campus cycling hub</a> to learn about the Campus Bike Centre, bike sharing and loan programs, showers and change rooms, lockers, route maps and more.</p>
<h3>Driving</h3>
<p>You must have a valid driver&#8217;s licence and insurance to drive a vehicle in British Columbia.&#160;Visit <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/international-experiences/living-in-victoria/getting-settled/index.php#ipn-get-your-identification">Get your identification</a> for more information. If you have questions, contact the Insurance Corporation of British Columbia (ICBC)&#160;more information.</p>
<p>UVic offers&#160;<a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/sustainability/topics/transportation/drivingalternatives/index.php">alternative driving options</a>&#160;including car sharing programs, you don't have your own car. We also have&#160;a <a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uvic.ca/security/parking/index.php">range of parking options</a>.</p>
<h3>Taxis</h3>
<p>Taxis in Victoria are operated by well-established companies that provide safe transportation and electronically metered fares.</p>
<ul>
<li><a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.taxicab.com/">BlueBird Cabs</a></li>
<li><a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://victoriataxi.com/">Victoria Taxi</a></li>
<li><a class="icoa icoa--out" href="http://www.yellowcabvictoria.com/">Yellow Cab</a></li>
<li><a class="icoa icoa--out" href="https://www.uber.com/global/en/cities/victoria/">Uber</a></li>
</ul>
                                                        </div>
